  "database": "rschema_0106",
  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0106, and it contains three tables: user, post, and comment. The user table has the following columns: user_id, username, email, password, user_type, activation_status, and creation_time. The user_id column is the primary key, and the other columns are not null. The post table has the following columns: post_id, post_title, post_description, image_path, thumbnail_path, activation_status, creation_time, and user_id. The post_id column is the primary key, and the other columns are not null. The comment table has the following columns: comment_content, author_id, post_id, and creation_time. The primary key is a composite key consisting of comment_creation_time, author_id, and post_id. The author_id and post_id columns are foreign keys that reference the user_id and post_id columns in the user and post tables, respectively. The foreign key constraints are set to cascade on delete and update.",
  "gold_question": "The database is an online forum or social media system where users can post and comment.\n\nMain functions\n\n1. User management\nUser registration: create a new user and record information such as username, email address, password, etc.\nUser login: verify username and password.\nUser information modification: allow users to modify personal information.\nUser activation status management: control whether users can use the system.\n\n2. Post management\nPost: users can post posts containing titles, descriptions, image paths, and thumbnail paths.\nPost status management: control whether posts are visible.\nPost browsing: users can view all visible posts.\nPost search: search for posts by title or description.\nPost deletion: users can delete their own posts, and administrators can delete any post.\n\n3. Comment management\nPost comments: users can comment on posts.\nComment browsing: users can view all comments on posts.\nComment deletion: users can delete their own comments, and administrators can delete any comment.\n\n4. Data association\nUser-post association: record the author of each post.\nUser-comment association: record the author of each comment.\nAssociation between posts and comments: Record all comments for each post.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0106.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0106\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `activation_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post` (\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `post_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `image_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `thumbnail_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `activation_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`post_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment` (\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`creation_time`, `author_id`, `post_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `post` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
